# rm304, the humming measure (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm304
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rmx_tage_slagworth
written_by codex
title the humming measure
fits stage=adult|old
prefers temper=calm honesty=guarded
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk measures_a_wait_with_the_length_of_a_quiet_sea_air
likes spiced_cider old_tales festival_bells first_snow
dislikes drizzle night_noise
fears a_jar_left_unstoppered a_rattle_behind_the_wall
hopes a_counter_with_a_shutter_of_its_own
topics work +0.5 pastimes +0.3 dreams +0.3 weather +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=quiet gossip=closed refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# measures a pause by humming a short sea air, lets cider spices settle completely, and lets questions settle even longer.

words
oath! = Cloves in the bung | Sink the high note
saying! = A measure can wait out a hurry | A jar remembers a careless lid
longair = my slow four-bar air | a tune with one long return
lowend = the low humming part | that final note
corkring = a soft ring of cork | a worn bung cut thin
scentcloth = a clean scrap of linen | a dry tasting cloth
ciderjaw = a little clove heat | warmth at the hinge of the jaw
lidspace = one small finger's width | a narrow gap
mugmark = a pale half-circle | a line left by a mug
stallshade = a shaded counter | a stall with a deep shutter
snowrim = white along an upper rim | a thin seam of snow
dripnoise = the slow ticking of drops | a clicking from a wet ledge
talestring = a tale with a long return | a story that comes back on itself

any
opinion @1 dole for 2 : Hungry wolves can't earn a dinner on an empty promise either. Give a dinner.
opinion @1 church for 1 : Nobody times a prayer in chapel. I value that.
opinion @1 houses against 2 : There's fine lettering on the closed side of too many doors.
opinion @1 strangers against 2 : Let a name settle in my memory before you ask me to open anything.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : The first peal lifts me. The shouting that follows puts me down again.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : I dislike sellers who tap a measure on the board until the buyer stops looking at it.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : From down in the Sump the city sounds different. You hear what keeps running after the doors shut.

grown
line @1 greet : I'll lay the tune aside. Speak.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : We've room for the length of an introduction.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The first sound carries a fair way.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. I heard your foot take the turn.
line @1 greet.return : That's my measure of quiet done, then.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : There's room in the tune for a familiar voice.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I'm mid-count. I'll listen between strokes.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : A low word carries comfortably tonight.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin may have the first word freely.
line @1 again.open : I remember where the measure broke off.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Over by the shutter, if you want me.
line @1 farewell : Keep the slow part for the walk back.
line @1 farewell.return : And a smooth ending to your own day.
line @1 react.news : Let the facts stand a breath once they're out.
line @1 react.news.new : That hadn't come within my hearing.
line @1 react.news.known : Heard it already. Same length, same notes.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That version runs longer than the facts I know.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Such a loss needs all the quiet it can get.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I'll mark that moment with the high note.
line @1 ask.how : Is anything pressing hard on you?
line @1 answer.how : I've got my breathing back to its usual time.
line @1 thank : A neat kindness. I will remember the measure of it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Barely cost me two notes.
line @1 sympathise : I can keep the room quiet for a little.
line @1 reassure : Nothing here needs to be settled in one breath.
line @1 decline : I've promised the quiet part of my evening elsewhere.
line @1 accept_decline : Then keep your time and I'll keep mine.
line @1 preclose : My last note's about used up for today.
line @1 accept_preclose : You've given this a fair hearing. Go easily.
scene air_measure
when topic=pastimes|work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #longair.capitalize# takes the length of a decent pause. | I slow #lowend# until I can feel my own breath again.
b : You always hum the same speed? | Have you gone short of air?
a : Near enough. My ears tell me when my temper's cheating. | Only of patience. This gets me some back.

scene jar_breath
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=none
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a smell left where the lid's clean belly meets the air. | I lay #scentcloth# flat before a tasting.
b : A good smell? | Why flat?
a : If there's any doubt, I'd want another nose on it. | A fold can hold yesterday's flavour. I'd like today's answer.

scene spiced_cider
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A good clove warms you after the cup has gone down. | More spice doesn't always mean a better cup.
b : Where do you feel it? | How do you judge it?
a : There. Right at my jaw. That's enough. | Can I still taste the apple? If I can, we may be getting somewhere.

scene festival_bells
when topic=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like the little gap between the bells practising and the feast beginning. | Bells are public music. My own bit stays below my breath.
b : Why the gap? | Don't they go together?
a : The whole day has drawn breath and hasn't shouted yet. | On a good morning, yes. Nobody has to know except me.

scene snow_first
when topic=weather here.weather=snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #snowrim.capitalize# changes the look of every lid. | First snow is quiet clear through.
b : Enough to cover a jar? | Clear? It's white.
a : Only enough to tell me which side the weather's coming from. | I mean I can hear a seam of silence down every street.

scene short_mist
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd sooner have honest rain than a fine damp clinging to my throat. | I can hear #dripnoise# long after the wind drops.
b : Wouldn't you be wetter? | Is it the actual dripping?
a : Probably. At least I'd know when it had stopped. | Sometimes. Sometimes the last drop gets stuck in my ears.

scene old_story
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_tales
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give me #talestring#. Let me forget the beginning for a minute. | A useful pause in a tale is one I don't have to fill.
b : Why forget it? | What if you guess the end?
a : Then the return feels as good as slipping into a coat that fits. | Then I enjoy waiting to hear how the teller gets there.

scene shutter_plan
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd save for a stall with one wall that shuts all the way across. | My counter would catch morning light and leave my face in shade.
b : Not for a bigger counter? | Shy of customers?
a : A day's work ought to have an ending. I'd buy the ending first. | Shy of being studied more closely than the goods.

scene late_tapping
when topic=home here.time=night
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : A loose shutter can repeat the same two notes clear through a night's rest. | The smallest noise at night gets steady while every other sound gives up.
b : Why don't you fix it? | You should try humming.
a : Happy to fix my own. I'm not traipsing through town in a nightshirt to fix the rest. | I do. I'd gladly give the shutter my part to sing.

scene hard_coin
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a little more distance between a day's pay and a day's hunger. | The small coins sound very grand in an empty jar.
b : Enough to get ahead? | Takes little to fill the air.
a : Enough to choose tomorrow's breakfast tonight. | Yes. The sound is rich and inconveniently brief.

scene tight_cork
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An old #corkring# can tell you whether a lid was ever forced. | A lid should come away clean enough to put back.
b : What does it say? | Even an empty jar?
a : Smooth on one side, torn on the other. That's a hand in too much hurry. | Especially an empty jar. I may need the smell of clean glass again.

scene closed_friends
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd let #self.friend# hear my little tune end to end. | A quiet drink would suit me beside #self.friend#.
b : Quite a privilege? | Quiet friendships last longer?
a : I reckon it is. I usually stop at the sound of company. | I've no notion. Quiet evenings feel longer, and I like that.

scene bay_air
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I'm looking across the Sound I let my sea tune go three beats farther. | A narrow street sends a hum back sharper than the bay does.
b : Why three? | Which suits you?
a : Enough to get somewhere between this shore and the next. | The bay. It lets me make a mistake privately.

scene wait_wheels
when topic=times|travel world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : All the waiting over late carts gets poured into a single shout when wheels show. | An empty stretch of road takes no time at all to inspect.
b : Have the wheels shown yet? | So why stand here?
a : No. Still room to keep one's ears out of the shouting. | The next look might bring a brimful cart. I haven't given up on it.

scene shy_market
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can wish a new arrival well without giving up my place in the queue. | I take a while to welcome anybody through a door.
b : Just a place? | How long?
a : That place cost part of a morning. | Long enough for a name to sound like a name and not a key trying a lock.

scene private_cork
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : There's a good reason I keep a lid on that story. | The name on that rumour isn't mine to spend.
b : Is it about a friend? | Is a name like coin?
a : It's about somebody who may have friends. That's plenty to go on. | No. You can usually get another copper.

scene public_words
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : The account from #world.news_from# was #world.news#. I kept it short. | #world.news#. That bit carried from #world.news_from#.
b : Where'd you shorten it? | Do you expect anything more?
a : At the end of what I heard. I took my own guess clean out. | I expect to listen if more comes. A useful small difference.

scene easy_cup
when topic=food|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn a mug by the handle instead of pushing it round the board. | I'd rather a plain chipped cup than a tall one which wobbles.
b : Why spare the board? | No fear of the chip?
a : I'm sparing the next drink. Nothing tips if the hand stays low. | Small chip on the far rim makes a better handle than most fancy handles.

story bung_skip [topic=memories]
  : I pressed a little dry cork onto a saucer full of water.
  : Cork leapt clean over the rim and stuck behind a button.
  b : Were you able to find it?
  : Only when my coat refused to close. Took me one wet saucer to teach a button to object.

story air_return [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : Once an echo sent my tune back so late I had already started the next one.
  : For three whole notes I thought some stranger knew the harmony.
  b : Were the notes any good?
  : Two good ones. On the third I had to agree to differ with myself.

story tall_cup [topic=food|memories]
  : I poured cider into a cup with a painted line halfway up the side.
  : Stopped at the line without thinking and put the jug away.
  b : Was it meant to mark a measure?
  : Part of a painted fence. A tall painted tree on my next cup bought me a far better helping.

rule @lip_cork
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dry round the shoulder. That one's properly shut.

rule @quiet_close
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let the silence get a good start on the next note.

rule @peal_carry
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A bell off in the distance counts for a full bar here.

rule @drizzle_gate
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Can't get rid of that little tick at the sill.

dlg @1 resident.hub : A plain word will carry well enough from there.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. Your voice fits where I remember it.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Speak easily. Darkness leaves plenty of room for sound.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : My patience will reach that far. I prefer to stay here.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.working=yes self.job=none] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Takes a good nose to know when to wait.
dlg @2 resident.job : I earn what I can and keep a careful measure of the time.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : From #world.news_from# I've kept this much: #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : You'd be asking me to loosen a lid I'd sooner keep tight.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Take the unhurried way if the day allows.
graft resident.hub
choice How long is the tune you're humming? -> air_length
node air_length
say Just long enough to take the edge off a hot mouthful. Learned that much of it before I ever had cause to remember the words.
choice What are the words now? -> air_words
choice I can hear the ending. -> hub
node air_words
say Still no words on my part. You could set anything to it. I'd hum softly so you could hear which way the tune meant to go.
choice I can work with a tune like that. -> hub
choice I'll carry the tune away. -> bye
